-- A clausal def is an ITEM MACRO, so a hole in a clause RHS is
-- elaborated once per generated item — the eliminator body, the
-- clause's equation lemma, the uniqueness lemma. Each is its own
-- goal, in its own context, and each is reported. They print under
-- the label the operator WROTE (`?step`, not `?dblS.step`): the
-- qualification is machine-made, and one written hole reading as one
-- name across its three derived obligations is the faithful account.
def dbl : ℕ → ℕ
  | dbl Z ≔ Z
  | dbl (S n) ≔ ?step
